            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for temptation, then the Marathi for greed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गर्व",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गर्व — garva — \"pride; conceit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बक्षीस मिळाल्याचा त्याला गर्व झाला. bakṣīs miḷālyācā tyālā garva jhālā. Winning the prize made him conceited."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often a fault: गर्व (garva) होणे, to grow conceited; गर्विष्ठ, arrogant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गर्व (garva) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit garva, \"pride, arrogance\" (CDIAL 4064)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
